@* The grab bar is the affordance, not the target: the drag is on the whole panel, so it works
   whether or not the bar is there. It is drawn for a top or bottom drawer only — on a side one it
   would be a vertical bar nobody has been taught to pull. *@
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
    <DrawerTrigger Target="drawer-handle">With a handle</DrawerTrigger>
    <Drawer Id="drawer-handle">
        <DrawerHeader><DrawerTitle>Pull it down</DrawerTitle>
            <DrawerDescription>Or drag anywhere on the panel.</DrawerDescription></DrawerHeader>
        <DrawerFooter><DrawerClose>Close</DrawerClose></DrawerFooter>
    </Drawer>

    <DrawerTrigger Target="drawer-nohandle">Without</DrawerTrigger>
    <Drawer Id="drawer-nohandle" ShowHandle="false">
        <DrawerHeader><DrawerTitle>Still draggable</DrawerTitle>
            <DrawerDescription>Nothing says so, which is the cost.</DrawerDescription></DrawerHeader>
        <DrawerFooter><DrawerClose>Close</DrawerClose></DrawerFooter>
    </Drawer>
</div>
